- All three former signal-11 cases terminate normally.

The ten P5-TB16 failures remain. P5-CB91–P5-CB98 also introduced twelve
source-level regressions reproduced by both the GitHub GCC package and the
independent Clang package:

- Phase 16: 4 regressions;
- Phase 17: 6 regressions;
- Milestone D: 2 additional regressions.

The authoritative ownership defect is a mismatch between two concepts:

- valid tracing may cross adjacent per-face local sheet charts through intrinsic
  source adjacency while remaining in one connected physical sheet/component;
- current arrangement/parity code requires one raw
  `(component, localSheetByFace)` pair across every boundary record.

This incorrectly rejects valid multi-face cells and cascades into topology and
simplification failures. The correction must introduce a canonical cell-side/
sheet equivalence class while retaining exact per-face local chart records. Do
not restore frequency voting or select a sheet by count/order.

## Random-bunny result

Four face-edge and four smooth-field processes are deterministic, terminate
normally, and pass the established wall and memory limits. Both paths still
fail closed without fallback or source-grid recovery at:

```text
NotProductionReady/completion
BoundaryParityRepair:MixedCellSourceScope
```

Typed evidence is deterministic:

- face-edge: cell `19`, halfedge/twin `21767/21766`, component values `[0,0]`,
  local chart values `[0,1]`, selected scope `-1/-1`, phase `preflight`;
- smooth: cell `45`, halfedge/twin `46451/46450`, component values `[0,0]`,
  local chart values `[0,1]`, selected scope `-1/-1`, phase `preflight`.

Both paths emit `0` vertices and `0` quads. Exact reuse/recompute remains `0/0`.
Memory timelines are deterministic and populated, but estimated simultaneous
ownership explains only **28.0–33.6%** of peak RSS.

